{"tool_name":"ciri-full","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"CIRI-full","home":"https://sourceforge.net/projects/ciri","license":"MIT","summary":"CircRNA Identifier. A de novo circular RNA identification tool.","addition_date":"2019-06-22T14:46:09Z","last_update_date":"2020-06-16T10:55:23Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:CIRI-full","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"zhangjinyang@biols.ac.cn","name":"Jinyang Zhang","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]},{"email":"zhfq@biols.ac.cn","name":"Fangqing Zhao","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]}],"documentation":[{"type":["General"],"url":"https://sourceforge.net/projects/ciri/files/CIRIquant/README.md/download"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Quantification","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3799"},{"term":"de Novo sequencing","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3644"},{"term":"trans-regulatory element prediction","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0443"}]}],"maturity":"Mature","name":"CIRI","operating_system":["Linux","Mac"],"owner":"Ruta","publication":[{"doi":"10.1186/s13073-019-0614-1","metadata":{"abstract":"\u00a9 2019 The Author(s).Currently, circRNA studies are shifting from the identification of circular transcripts to understanding their biological functions. However, such endeavors have been limited by large-scale determination of their full-length sequences and also by the inability of accurate quantification at the isoform level. Here, we propose a new feature, reverse overlap (RO), for circRNA detection, which outperforms back-splice junction (BSJ)-based methods in identifying low-abundance circRNAs. By combining RO and BSJ features, we present a novel approach for effective reconstruction of full-length circRNAs and isoform-level quantification from the transcriptome. We systematically compared the difference between the BSJ-level and isoform-level differential expression analyses using human liver tumor and normal tissues and highlight the necessity of deepening circRNA studies to the isoform-level resolution. The CIRI-full software can be accessed at https://sourceforge.net/projects/ciri.","authors":[{"name":"Chen S."},{"name":"Hou L."},{"name":"Ji P."},{"name":"Zhao F."},{"name":"Zheng Y."}],"citationCount":43,"date":"2019-01-19T00:00:00Z","journal":"Genome Medicine","title":"Reconstruction of full-length circular RNAs enables isoform-level quantification"},"pmcid":"PMC6339429","pmid":"30660194","type":["Primary"]}],"topic":[{"term":"Functional, regulatory and non-coding RNA","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0659"},{"term":"Gene transcripts","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3512"},{"term":"RNA splicing","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3320"}]},"bioschemas":{"name":"CIRI","home":"https://bio.tools/CIRI-full","license":"MIT","summary":"CircRNA Identifier. A de novo circular RNA identification tool.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:ciri-full/cmd/sourceforge.net","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"distribution":{"sourcecode":{"interpreted":true}},"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"documentation":{"general":true},"license":{"open_source":true,"osi":true},"publications":[{"entries":[{"cit_count":103,"citations":[{"count":4,"year":"2026"},{"count":5,"year":"2019"},{"count":13,"year":"2024"},{"count":13,"year":"2025"},{"count":14,"year":"2020"},{"count":15,"year":"2023"},{"count":19,"year":"2021"},{"count":20,"year":"2022"}],"doi":"10.1186/s13073-019-0614-1","pmcid":"PMC6339429","pmid":"30660194","ref_count":42,"refs":[{"count":1,"year":"2002"},{"count":2,"year":"2011"},{"count":2,"year":"2012"},{"count":3,"year":"2014"},{"count":4,"year":"2013"},{"count":4,"year":"2018"},{"count":5,"year":"2016